      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T14:57:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ask Nicolas :) My understanding is that the logic was implemented in a practical manner: the runtime images are mainly to speed up app startup after a Mainline update, where apps are usually in the `verify` state. Apps in `speed-profile` have app images (.art files) generated by dexopt, which is the same type of thing as runtime images, so they don\u0027t need runtime images. Apps in `speed` or `run-from-apk` are rare, so we don\u0027t bother to care (although in theory we can use runtime images for them and I don\u0027t see why we don\u0027t).",
